## What (Stack & Structure)

**Stack**: WordPress {{WP_VERSION}}, PHP {{PHP_VERSION}} (WordPress supports 7.4+, 8.3+ recommended), Composer, `@wordpress/scripts` for block/JS builds, `@wordpress/env` (wp-env) for local environments

### Project Structure
```
my-plugin/
├── my-plugin.php       # Plugin header (Requires at least / Requires PHP), bootstrap
├── uninstall.php       # Cleanup on uninstall
├── composer.json       # Autoload (PSR-4), WPCS, PHPStan, PHPUnit polyfills
├── package.json        # @wordpress/scripts, @wordpress/env
├── .wp-env.json        # Local WordPress environment
├── includes/ (src/)    # Namespaced PHP classes (hooks, REST, services)
├── src/blocks/<name>/  # block.json (apiVersion 3), edit.js, render.php
├── languages/          # .pot / translations (text domain = plugin slug)
└── tests/              # PHPUnit (WP_UnitTestCase), Jest, Playwright e2e
```
Block themes follow the same spirit: `theme.json`, `templates/`, `parts/`, `patterns/`.

## Why (Purpose & Organization)

### Architecture: hooks-driven plugin/theme with namespaced services
- **Hooks**: behaviour attaches through actions and filters registered in one place
- **Namespaces and prefixes**: every function, class, option, hook and handle is namespaced or prefixed
- **Blocks first**: UI built as blocks (`block.json` apiVersion 3), server rendering via `render.php`
- **REST**: custom endpoints through `register_rest_route()` with a mandatory `permission_callback`
- Keep logic in plain classes testable without a full request; thin hook callbacks
- General PHP: see the `php` stack

See `rules/02-architecture-wordpress.md` for complete patterns.

### Critical Rules
| Rule | Reason |
|------|--------|
| Capability check + nonce on every state change | Prevents privilege escalation and CSRF |
| Sanitize on input, escape on output (`esc_html`, `esc_attr`, `esc_url`, `wp_kses_post`) | Prevents XSS |
| `$wpdb->prepare()` for every query with variable data | Prevents SQL injection |
| `permission_callback` on every REST route | Routes without it are publicly accessible |
| `defined( 'ABSPATH' ) \|\| exit;` in every PHP file | Blocks direct file access |
| Prefix/namespace everything, text domain on every string | Avoids collisions, enables translation |
| WPCS (PHPCS) + PHPStan clean | Code quality and consistent style |
| 80%+ coverage, tests run through wp-env | Quality assurance |

